WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:05.600
British actor Tom Ellis is having one hell
of a time playing the lead role in TV's Lucifer,

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.820
a police procedural which follows the devil
himself as he retires to the City of Angels

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.799
and teams up with LAPD detective, Chloe Decker.

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:17.860
So, with Lucifer back on our screens, let's
take a look at 7 crazy facts about the devilish

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.500
show.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.430
Tom Ellis may play the former Lord of Hell
in Lucifer, but in real life, he actually

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:25.610
grew up in a very religious family.

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:30.460
Ellis's father is a Baptist pastor, as are
Ellis's sister, brother-in-law, and uncle.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:34.180
And when they heard he was making this show,
they were very excited for him.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:39.170
Ellis says he sees Lucifer as a satirical
"story of redemption" rather than "a big theological

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:41.309
debate."

00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:45.219
Well before the show had even aired, it was
already the target of protests, with several

00:00:45.219 --> 00:00:49.430
organisations petitioning the show's network
Fox to cancel the series completely.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:54.129
A petition the American Family Association's
website One Million Moms, which gathered 38,000

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:58.399
signatures, said the show 'mischaracterised
and glorified Satan' and that if Fox went

00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:02.479
ahead with their plans to air Lucifer, the
network would be 'disrespecting Christianity'

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:03.710
and 'mocking the Bible'.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:07.530
This isn't the first time the world of Lucifer
has caused controversy though.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:11.780
Author Neil Gaiman's Sandman graphic novel,
which the TV show is loosely based on along

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.691
with the spin-off comic Lucifer, also drew
fire from the American Family Association

00:01:15.691 --> 00:01:16.870
back in 1991.

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:24.150
Not only has the series inspired anti-Lucifer
protests, it's also inspired pro-Lucifer graffiti!

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:29.080
Yes, in keeping with the show's devilish spirit,
someone in LA or perhaps more than one person,

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.500
took it upon themselves to spray-paint the
words 'Watch Lucifer' on top of billboards

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.980
advertising other networks' shows such as
NBC's Shades of Blue.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:42.520
And they even added a set of horns to actors
featuring on those billboards including Jennifer

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:43.520
Lopez!

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:47.130
Tom Ellis says he doesn't know who did it
and he doesn't condone it, but he does find

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:48.360
it very funny!

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:53.210
When author Neil Gaiman created the character
of Lucifer in The Sandman graphic novels,

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:58.600
he was inspired by David Bowie; however, after
reading the show's scripts, Tom Ellis saw

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:03.160
Lucifer as an Oscar Wilde or Noel Coward character
with added rock n roll spirit.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.470
So, he approached Lucifer as if the character
were the lovechild of Noel Coward and Mick

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:10.640
Jagger with a dash of British actor Terry
Thomas.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.319
The TV show still tips its hat to Bowie's
influence on the original comic books though

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:16.430
by featuring his music.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:20.650
As for choosing Lucifer's accent, according
to Ellis, when he tried an American accent,

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:24.489
the character came off as a jerk, but with
an English accent he found that Lucifer could

00:02:24.489 --> 00:02:30.420
get away with saying all sorts of terrible
things and still come across as rather charming.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.050
As music is such a big part of the show, what
with Lucifer running a nightclub and singing

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.099
and playing the piano, Ellis decided to make
a special playlist for his character which

00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:41.989
he listened to during his downtime to help
him get into the part.

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:45.719
His playlist features a mix of tracks that
appear in the series, such as David Bowie's

00:02:45.719 --> 00:02:50.629
Fame and Rebel Rebel, as well as Ellis's own
picks including Purple Haze by Jimi Hendrix

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:52.450
and Ring of Fire by Johnny Cash.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.620
Lucifer's showrunner Joe Henderson has even
been known to listen to Ellis's playlist while

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.420
writing scripts.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:03.040
In fact, Devil's Haircut by Beck was actually
on Ellis's playlist before it made it into

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:04.180
the show's pilot episode!

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.499
By the way, Ellis comes from quite a musical
family himself.

00:03:07.499 --> 00:03:12.099
His mother was a music teacher, his dad did
amateur operatics, and all his siblings grew

00:03:12.099 --> 00:03:16.349
up playing instruments, with Ellis playing
trumpet and then French horn in orchestras

00:03:16.349 --> 00:03:19.340
during his teenage years.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:23.560
When Tricia Helfer was cast as Lucifer's mother
Charlotte for the show's second season, Tom

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:28.599
Ellis was blown away as not only is he a massive
Battlestar Galactica fan, but he also used

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:32.549
to have a crush on the Canadian actress who
played Number Six in the award-winning sci-fi

00:03:32.549 --> 00:03:33.549
series.

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:37.560
In fact, although Helfer plays Lucifer's mother
in the show, in real life she's just four

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:42.370
years older than Ellis and she's actually
five years younger than DB Woodside who plays

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:44.189
her other on-screen son, Amenadiel!

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:48.650
Ellis has joked that it's all a bit weird
and oedipal and that he and DB both feel like

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:52.319
Stifler from the American Pie movies!

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:56.319
While they were filming at Long Beach for
season one's seventh episode "Wingman", the

00:03:56.319 --> 00:04:01.599
shoot was repeatedly interrupted by a random
drone flying around the cast and crew.

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:05.519
Eventually, the show's security tracked down
the guy who was flying the drone, but he refused

00:04:05.519 --> 00:04:06.519
to stop!

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:11.150
So, actor DB Woodside marched down the beach
to confront the drone pilot guy who then tried

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:15.900
to make a speedy getaway in his car as Woodside
knocked on his door, asking to speak with

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:16.900
him.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.299
It was only later that Woodside realised just
what he must have looked like in his full

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:21.109
Amenadiel costume at the time!

00:04:21.109 --> 00:04:24.740
So guys, what are you most looking forward
to about the new season of Lucifer?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.409
And what's been your favourite part of the
show so far?

